# Suppressions are the exception, not the habit. Each entry states why the code
# path is unreachable here and what has to happen before the line can be deleted.

# fast-uri 3.1.2 — Unicode hostname canonicalisation bypass.
#
# Reached only as @prisma/client -> prisma -> @prisma/dev -> @prisma/streams-local
# -> ajv -> fast-uri. That ajv instance validates Prisma's own internal config
# schemas; no request data and no runtime code path in this service reaches it.
# Patched releases exist (3.1.4, 4.1.1) but nothing in this repo can select them:
# npm ignores the `overrides` block in this workspace, and pinning fast-uri
# directly only adds a nested copy while the hoisted 3.1.2 that ajv resolves
# stays put — verified by building the prod-deps image and reading both copies.
#
# Remove when a Prisma release pulls a patched fast-uri transitively.
CVE-2026-13676
CVE-2026-16221

# sharp 0.34.5 — inherited libvips vulnerabilities.
#
# The advisory scopes the impact to "those processing untrusted input". This app
# imports next/image zero times and configures no remotePatterns, so nothing is
# ever handed to the optimiser: sharp is present only because Next installs it as
# an optional dependency. It cannot be upgraded on its own either, since Next
# 16.2.11 declares sharp ^0.34.5, which excludes the fixed 0.35.0.
#
# Remove when Next widens that range to a patched sharp.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
